Sprint 14 — Hardening

IKM-14.1 — Security & Resilience

Goal

Protect the application from brute-force attacks, misconfigurations, and standard web vulnerabilities before deploying to production.

Description

Introduce fundamental security middleware and strict rate limiting.

Acceptance Criteria

 Install and configure helmet globally in main.ts for secure HTTP headers.

 Configure enableCors() in main.ts with strict origin rules (read from env configuration).

 Implement @nestjs/throttler.

 Apply strict rate limits globally (e.g., 100 requests per minute).

 Apply ultra-strict rate limits specifically on POST /auth/login (e.g., 5 requests per minute per IP) to prevent password guessing.

IKM-14.2 — Database Indexes & Final Walkthrough

Goal

Guarantee dashboard and reporting performance at scale, and verify the entire end-to-end system.

Description

Analyze the query patterns generated in Sprints 1-10 and write a final SQL migration to apply B-Tree indexes to heavily queried foreign keys and status columns. Finally, execute an integration script simulating a full month lifecycle.

Acceptance Criteria

 Migration created adding indexes to: members(user_id), monthly_obligations(member_id, status), contribution_payments(member_id, status, payment_date), penalties(member_id, status).

 test-full-platform-flow.sh script is provided that: logs in as admin, creates a member, generates an obligation, submits a payment as member, approves the payment as admin, and finally fetches the member's statement, confirming a 200 OK at every single step.
